Lesson Set 04 — Orientation, Shock & Tilt Awareness
IMU (MPU-6050) + Vibration Switches + Tilt Switch on Arduino Nano
Course Introduction Document • DroidWorks U.S.A.
1. Purpose of This Lesson Set
Up to this point the droid has learned to notice movement (PIR + RCWL) and measure distance
(ultrasonic / ToF). Those sensors answer the question “Is something moving near me?” and “How far
away is it?”
Lesson Set 04 answers a different set of questions the droid needs in order to behave like a coherent
character:
• Which way am I oriented? (upright, leaning, tipped)
• Am I accelerating or being moved?
• Did something just hit or bump me hard?
• Is my body currently tilted beyond a safe angle?
These capabilities form the foundation for later head tracking, reactive “ouch” behaviors, safer
movement, and richer fused state that can drive sound, lights, and motion.
